      <h4>Tax percentage variability within countries warrants methodological scrutiny</h4>
      <p>The dataset exhibits high week-to-week variability in tax percentages within individual countries (e.g., the United States shows 27.6%–62.3% within the first month). This likely reflects estimation methodology rather than true policy changes. Analysts building subsidy/tax calibration models should treat tax_percentage as a directional indicator rather than a precise policy variable, and should cross-validate against official regulatory filings before using in quantitative models.</p>
